<title>MEXICO: Mexico union movement sells off bean mountain.</title>
<headline>Mexico union movement sells off bean mountain.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's largest union movement will start Thursday to sell off 380,000 tonnes of dry beans at below market prices, a union source said.</p>
<p>Mexican Workers' Confederation (CTM), the umbrella group for most of the country's unions, will sell the beans to members at 5.5 pesos per kilo, a CTM official said. Market prices are up to 7 pesos per kilo.</p>
<p>The confederation bought the beans last month from growers in the northern state of Zacatecas in a bid to give members access to cheaper basic foods.</p>
<p>Plans also are to sell rice to members at prices lower than market levels, the official added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
